      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Focusing on non-verbal communication is crucial, as body language and personal space norms vary significantly across cultures. Understanding differences in direct vs. indirect communication styles can also prevent misunderstandings during questioning. Additionally, awareness of religious or cultural practices that might influence reactions to police presence is a vital area to cover in your training. This heightened cultural sensitivity can significantly improve rapport and reduce the perceived threat level.",
